            }
          },
          {
            "name": "huaweicloud_sandbox_exec_poll",
            "description": "Poll an async sandbox task started by huaweicloud_sandbox_exec_one_shot with mode: \"async\". One call runs a bounded server-side wait (wait_ms 0-60000: sleep-2 intervals checking the task's status file; the exec timeout auto-folds to wait_ms + 15s so the wait always fits), then returns the task's verdict as a discriminated union — done (exitCode + logTail: the command finished), running (logTail: keep polling), lost (the wrapper died without an exit status, or the task directory vanished — a sandbox reboot — while this process remembered the task; restart with a new task_id if needed), never (the task was claimed but never launched — the start exec died between claim and spawn; start a NEW task_id, a same-id retry can never spawn), unknown (no task directory and no memory of the task_id — it never started here, or both the sandbox and this agent restarted). logTail is the last tail_bytes (default 4096) of the task's captured stdout+stderr. The retry ladder: started:\"uncertain\" → retry the SAME task_id (the claim file blocks a second copy); started:\"dup\" + verdict \"never\" → new task_id.",
