          {
            "name": "huaweicloud_sandbox_expose_tunnel",
            "description": "Expose a port on the sandbox to a public DevBridge tunnel URL (devbridge 0.2.x). Authenticates automatically (DevBridge auth is fixed to API Key — AK/SK login removed: the waterfall reads the sandbox keyring, then the /tmp/hw_api_key file channel; when both are empty it auto-creates the per-account × per-pool key (devkit-ephemeral/devkit-persistent) via the DevStation relay API and injects it, reporting authMode API_KEY_AUTO), selectively cleans only same-port/orphan tunnels before exposing (cleanup_mode=stale default — other ports, other sessions and keepalive-protected tunnels are preserved, except a tunnel bound to THIS port, which is always replaced; on 10006 quota it removes orphans first, then the oldest non-keepalive tunnel one at a time), starts the host detached from the exec session (setsid/nohup/disown so it survives session teardown), extracts the public URL (https://<id>-<port>.devbridge-s2.hwtunnel.com), and health-checks it before returning. Use the ACTUAL port reported by huaweicloud_sandbox_deploy_nginx (its \"port\" field auto-increments on conflict) — never the originally requested port. This automates the manual \"Expose the deployed app\" flow (huawei-sandbox skill). Returns ok, publicUrl, port, tunnelId, authMode, expiresAt (expiry_hours lifetime, default 72h; 1-720), keepalive.enrolled/tunnelCount/watchdogPid, warnings, sandboxLifetime and urlLifetimeHint. The urlLifetimeHint MUST be relayed to the developer together with the URL: the tunnel expiry is NOT the sandbox lifetime — an idle sandbox shuts down (ephemeral also auto-deletes), which kills the URL. AUTO-ENROLLS the tunnel into the keepalive watchdog (unattended renewal + host re-attach + health check; pass keepalive:false to opt out). The URL is re-verified from a second independent exec session: persistent/verifyHttpCode distinguish a session-surviving URL from one that dies with the deploying session, and a non-persistent URL carries a 请勿分享 warning. Gateway-level tunnel errors (404 \"tunnel not found\" / \"port not configured\", 502 \"bad gateway\") are classified by exact body — an app's own 404/502 page is never mistaken for them. When no usable URL is reachable after retries it returns ok:false instead of a dead URL; when the tunnel quota (10006) stays full after the selective cleanup it returns ok:false with error_code devbridge_tunnel_quota_exceeded (keepalive-protected tunnels are preserved — remove unused tunnels or retry with cleanup_mode=all for a full reset). When auto-creation hits the 20-key quota it returns ok:false with error_code HDKIT_DEVBRIDGE_KEY_QUOTA_EXCEEDED, the currentKeys list, and the console cleanup URL; a failed key invalidation self-heals by clearing the cache and recreating before the next probe. The auto-create relay goes through hdkitservice and inherits its 409 HDKIT_VERSION_TOO_OLD version gate: an outdated plugin fails auto-create the same way it fails connect, and the expose failure carries error_code HDKIT_VERSION_TOO_OLD with the upgrade remediation under gateRemediation, and clientVersion and minVersion when the service sends them — upgrade the plugin instead of creating a key by hand.",
            "inputSchema": {
              "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "port": {
                  "description": "Port nginx actually serves on — use the \"port\" value returned by huaweicloud_sandbox_deploy_nginx, not the originally requested port.",
                  "type": [
                    "number",
                    "string",
                    "null"
                  ]
                },
                "expiry_hours": {
                  "description": "Tunnel lifetime in hours, 1-720 (default 72). 720 = the devbridge 30-day maximum; the keepalive watchdog renews to 720h daily.",
                  "type": [
                    "number",
                    "string",
                    "null"
                  ]
                },
                "keepalive": {
                  "description": "Enroll the tunnel into the keepalive watchdog (default true — pass false to opt out). Returns keepalive.enrolled/tunnelCount/watchdogPid.",
                  "type": "boolean"
                },
                "cleanup_mode": {
                  "description": "Tunnel cleanup before exposing. stale (default): delete same-port tunnels + orphan records/hosts; preserve other ports, other sessions and keepalive-protected tunnels — except a tunnel bound to THIS port, which is always replaced. all: wipe every tunnel/host (manual full reset only — a shared sandbox loses every session's tunnels). none: no cleanup (a stale same-port host can then conflict).",
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "stale",
                    "all",
                    "none"
