          {
            "name": "huaweicloud_sandbox_connect",
            "description": "Connect to a sandbox via hdkitservice. One instance per user per pool — reuses the same-pool sandbox if available, otherwise creates a new one. Quota: 1 instance per pool type (a user may hold 1 ephemeral AND 1 persistent simultaneously; same-type requests reuse the existing instance). On quota exhaustion the API returns HTTP 429 with one of three codes: HDKIT_QUOTA_EXCEEDED (retry useless — release or reuse the existing instance; Retry-After 60), HDKIT_TEMPLATE_QUOTA_EXCEEDED (the running instances of this account for this sandbox type are at the limit — shut down or release an instance of the same type and retry; no Retry-After), or HDKIT_CAPACITY_INSUFFICIENT (pool capacity; retry later / off-peak; Retry-After 60). Gateway 502/504 timeouts during orchestration are retried automatically (30s/45s backoff) — the server may already have created the instance, so a retry reuses it. An outdated plugin version is rejected by the 409 HDKIT_VERSION_TOO_OLD version gate, surfaced by the sandbox tools (connect/check_user/sign_agreement/credentials) as ok:false and by the voucher trio as claimed:false, always carrying code, message, and remediation naming the upgrade act (npx --yes huaweicloud-devkit@latest update --target <agent>, restart the agent session, or huaweicloud_upgrade), with clientVersion and minVersion present when the service sends them. Returns session_id, dev_stage_id, connection_id, connection_address, expiresAt (STS credential expiry), pool_type/resolved template_id echo, server-configured lifecycle numbers (pool_idle_shutdown_minutes / pool_idle_delete_minutes / pool_reclaim_minutes) and started (true when a reused instance was woken from shutdown). Lifecycle hints are announced only on the first connect of a session or when started=true. Ephemeral pool (default): idle auto-shutdown after 30min, auto-delete after 1h — do not keep important data there. Persistent pool: data disk retained (EVS 32G), idle shutdown after 1h, idle reclaim capped at 7 days. Numbers are configured by hdkitservice; the text follows the server echo and falls back to these defaults. Vendor-gated (vendorConfirmed): call only when the vendor is established — see the vendorConfirmed parameter description; when unknown, ask which cloud the user means first.",
            "inputSchema": {
