            "name": "huaweicloud_gateway_call",
            "description": "Call one open-mcp gateway tool generically with tool and toolArgs — the single face for every gateway tool. Read-only discovery (no credentials): search_apis (query; optional limit/category) finds products by entity keywords when none is named; list_products (optional category/keyword) and get_product (product; optional include_sops) cover the product dimension (category, is_global — include_sops adds full SOP texts); list_apis (product; optional tag/search/limit/offset/include_sops) lists one product's API catalog with tag_groups; get_api (product, api; optional region) returns full API documentation — parameter types/enums, x-constraint preconditions, response schema, region endpoint — a must-read before any call; get_api_examples (product, api; optional region) returns official request examples. Discovery chain: search_apis → list_apis → get_api → get_api_examples. execute_api, manage_policy, query_data, and transform_data are delegated to the gateway's own policy engine: the first call forwards immediately, and when the engine refuses, its reason names the grant options — confirm the grant with the user in conversation after the refusal (a standing go-ahead for the task is not consent for a policy write), grant with manage_policy add using an ephemeral scope (once/session/temporary), then retry the call. Permanent grants are an operator policy-file edit (hot-reload). Denied outright, no grant path: secret operations, file targets inside devkit state, non-canonical manage_policy action/scope spellings, permanent-scope add, ttl_seconds on add or remove, remove with scope, and tool names outside the devkit's static vocabulary.",
